ght-to-pee/126938","site":"T Nation · 106 posts · 2009"},{"title":"Nas' New Album","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/nas-new-album/109405","site":"T Nation · 105 posts · 2008"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Cryotherapy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryotherapy"},{"title":"Green tea","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_tea"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Facial fat & puffiness","chain":["Cold plus green tea on skin","Vessels narrow, skin calms","Temporarily less puffy face"],"effect":"claimed","text":"Frozen brewed green tea rubbed on the face is meant to narrow vessels and calm skin for a temporarily less puffy look. The routine spread on social media, and it has not been tested for this use."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Facial icing with green tea ice cubes is a social media skincare practice in which frozen brewed green tea is rubbed on the face, with proponents citing reduced puffiness and calmer skin.","No studies found on this practice. Wikipedia describes general cold therapy as agreed to relieve symptoms like swelling with study results that conflict, and notes that green tea compounds have no proven biological effects in humans [1][2]."],"infobox":[["Type","Topical home practice"],["Ingredients","Brewed green tea, ice"],["Related","Cryotherapy"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Practitioners brew green tea, freeze it in trays and apply the cubes to the face, often in the morning, in the belief that cold plus tea antioxidants reduce redness and puffiness."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found. Studies of ice packs on injuries report short-term pain relief, with limited long-term evidence [1]. Adverse events from cold therapy are suspected to be underreported [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks","paras":["General cold therapy sources note frostbite risk with extreme cold and listed contraindications such as Raynaud syndrome and poor circulation or sensation [1]. Green tea extracts can cause skin reactions in some people [2]."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Cryotherapy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryotherapy","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Green tea","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_tea","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Cryotherapy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryotherapy","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"More Trouble Than I Am Worth: Chaos Is The Plan (T3hPwnisher Log)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-trouble-than-i-am-worth-chaos-is-the-plan-t3hpwnisher-log/276232","site":"T Nation · 8674 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Rising From the Ashes (CL)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/rising-from-the-ashes-cl/233718","site":"T Nation · 6788 posts · 2017"},{"title":"Just. Don't. Suck. Vol. 2","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/just-dont-suck-vol-2/273858","site":"T Nation · 1734 posts · 2021"},{"title":"The Quote Game","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-quote-game/65604","site":"T Nation · 1182 posts · 2006"},{"title":"NBA 2012 - 2013","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/nba-2012-2013/183080","site":"T Nation · 1126 posts · 2012"},{"title":"Grettiron's Training Log","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/grettirons-training-log/129760","site":"T Nation · 1126 posts · 2011"}]}